{
  "requirement": "`habeas mdbook` MUST NOT generate per-test coverage subchapters or captured-source\npages under the execution-coverage chapter of\n{cite}`requirements.test-coverage.index`. File-notes pages supporting coverage\ngap explanations under {cite}`requirements.test-coverage.index.file_map.notes`\nMUST remain available.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations in `requirements.test-coverage.index.details`**\n1. `habeas mdbook` MUST NOT generate per-test coverage subchapters under the documented-coverage chapter.\n2. It MUST NOT generate captured-source pages under that chapter.\n3. File-notes pages MUST remain available.\n\n**Coverage of the two MUST NOT clauses**\n- `src/execution_coverage/book.rs#mod[tests]/fn[book_ignores_saved_measurements_and_preserves_artifacts]` is the key test. It writes a saved measurement attempt, which has a test name and profraw data, and then populates the book.\n- The test asserts that the chapter list is exactly `[\"Documented coverage gaps\", \"File notes: code.rs\"]`. A per-test subchapter or a captured-source page would add a chapter, so this assertion rejects both.\n- It asserts that no chapter content contains the saved test name and no chapter content has a `<select`.\n- It asserts that no chapter path contains `-source`.\n- It repeats the check with invalid and empty `attempt.json` files. The rendered output stays identical to the output without saved measurements.\n- It asserts that the overview omits \"Captured source\", \"Test runs and provenance\", and \"selected test attempts\".\n\n**Coverage of the \"remain available\" clause**\n- `src/execution_coverage/book.rs#mod[tests]/fn[documented_items_are_counted_once_with_browsable_directory_and_file_groups]` checks the file-notes pages. It has five documented files, and it asserts exactly five chapters whose names start with \"File notes:\".\n- For `code.rs`, `src/direct.rs` and `src/deep/nested.rs`, it asserts that each note page exists at the expected path. The page content contains `File: <code>{file}</code>` and the `coverage-note-N` anchors, and the card links to them.\n- It also checks that the file-notes chapter is listed in the first test's output (`File notes: code.rs`).\n- `src/execution_coverage/book.rs#mod[tests]/fn[generated_reports_inherit_the_requirements_index_hierarchy]` checks that the generated coverage chapter's sub-items are pages with the right parent names and numbers. They link back to `../coverage.html`, and they hold in both numbered and unnumbered parent cases.\n\n**Conclusion**\nThe tests cover each obligation with assertions that would reject the forbidden pages and a missing notes page. All three tests carry `{test}` references to the subject. I found no gap.",
